{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Days.</b> Two." "<b>Many.</b> Three. From here the Sages said: one does not besiege cities of the nations fewer than three days before the Sabbath. And it teaches that one opens with peace for two or three days, and so it says, ״וַיֵּשֶׁב דָּוִד בְּצִקְלָג יָמִים שְׁנָיִם״ (II Samuel 1); and it is speaking of an optional war. (Sifrei)" "<b>For is the tree of the field a man.</b> See — כִּי serves in the sense of 'perhaps': perhaps the man of the field — to enter within the siege because of you, to suffer the suffering of hunger and thirst like the people of the city? Why would you destroy it?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:51.064724559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}